{
  "strategy": "The video appears to show a single static geometry diagram. Gather one clear question-state frame, then use structured visual reading plus OCR to extract the diagram facts and labels needed to derive the shaded-area expression from the geometry rather than guessing from the answer choices.",
  "tool_calls": [
    {
      "step": 1,
      "tool": "frame_retriever",
      "arguments": {
        "video_path": "VIDEO",
        "query": "original geometry problem diagram with a circle centered at O, points P Q and R on the circumference, red shaded regions, and the radius label 6, before any explanation overlay",
        "timestamps": null,
        "num_frames": 3
      },
      "purpose": "Retrieve the main problem frame(s) showing the complete diagram and visible labels.",
      "depends_on": []
    },
    {
      "step": 2,
      "tool": "ocr",
      "arguments": {
        "frame_path": "<STEP_1:frames>",
        "timestamp": null
      },
      "purpose": "Read the on-screen problem text and numeric labels such as the radius 6 and the condition involving P, Q, and R.",
      "depends_on": [
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "step": 3,
      "tool": "chart_analyzer",
      "arguments": {
        "frame_path": "<STEP_1:frames>",
        "timestamp": null,
        "query": "geometry diagram structure: identify the full circle, center O, points P Q and R on the circumference, the equal triangle formed by connecting P Q and R, the three red leaf-shaped regions, and which arcs bound each shaded region"
      },
      "purpose": "Extract the geometric structure of the figure so the refiner can determine what shapes compose the red area and which lengths/angles are implied.",
      "depends_on": [
        1
      ]
    }
  ],
  "refinement_instructions": "Write a fresh trace from scratch. Use the retrieved frame as the authoritative question-state evidence. From OCR, cite the exact visible givens: the circle centered at O, radius OP = 6, and the condition PQ = QR = RP with P, Q, R on the circle and serving as centers of arcs through O. From chart_analyzer, cite the structural facts: P, Q, R form an equilateral triangle inscribed in the circle, so each central angle subtending a side is 120 degrees; each red leaf is the overlap between two 60-degree sectors of radius 6 centered at adjacent circumference points and can be computed as two 60-degree sectors minus two equilateral triangles, or equivalently as one lens area. Then derive the total shaded area carefully and explicitly before mapping to the options. Preserve provenance in the rewritten trace by attributing visible labels/text to OCR and diagram structure to chart_analyzer. If the computed expression contradicts any prior assumption, update the answer accordingly. Do not guess from symmetry alone; show the intermediate geometry and the final option match."
}
